// Q-095 `for x in xs => { ... } | flatten()` pipes each round's block, not the list: a list of lists comes out, and `quillo check` says nothing
// mode: run
// open-when: [[1, 10], [2, 20]]
// fixed-when: /warning|\[1, 10, 2, 20\]/
// From FEEDBACK14.md §Q-095 (found on 991e96c). In JavaScript `xs.map((n) => { ... }).flat()`
// flattens the list; here the `|` after the block's `}` belongs to the body. Quillo Coop's
// salary deduction batch was a list of lists, and failed later, elsewhere, with
// "list has no field `member_id`".

let pairs = for n in [1, 2] => {
    let tens = n * 10
    [n, tens]
} | flatten()
print(pairs)
